# UI & Frontend Patterns ✅

## Application Architecture

### Three-View System
The app uses a managed view system with `AppView` type:
```typescript
type AppView = "chat" | "settings" | "devtools";
const [currentView, setCurrentView] = useState<AppView>("chat");
```

### Main Components
- **[src/Bar.tsx](mdc:src/Bar.tsx)**: Main floating bar UI with state management
- **[src/App.tsx](mdc:src/App.tsx)**: Full chat interface with settings integration
- **[src/components/Settings.tsx](mdc:src/components/Settings.tsx)**: Settings configuration
- **[src/components/DevToolsPanel.tsx](mdc:src/components/DevToolsPanel.tsx)**: Developer tools

## Voice Interaction UI States

### Bar State Management
```typescript
// Voice mode differentiation
const [isSpacebarDictation, setIsSpacebarDictation] = useState(false);
const [barState, setBarState] = useState<BarState>("default");

// State mappings:
// "dictating" - Orange microphone (spacebar mode)
// "listening" - Blue microphone (agent mode)
// "transcribing" - Green microphone (processing)
// "speaking" - TTS playback
```

### Event Listeners Pattern
```typescript
useEffect(() => {
    const setupListeners = async () => {
        // Spacebar dictation events
        unlistenSpacebarStart = await listen("spacebar-transcription-start", () => {
            setIsSpacebarDictation(true);
            setBarState("dictating");
        });

        // Agent mode events
        unlistenAgentStart = await listen("app-dictation-started", () => {
            setIsSpacebarDictation(false);
            setBarState("listening");
        });
    };

    const cleanup = setupListeners();
    return () => {
        cleanup?.then(unlisten => unlisten?.());
    };
}, []);
```

